  "strategy": "1. Approach and Rationale\n\nThe proposed strategy combines smoothness with adaptive constraint handling tobreak the monotonicity assumed in the previous periodic solutions. Unlike treatingh(x) as piecewise-constant over fixed blocks, this approach seekscontinuous, smooth solutions with carefully crafted correlations. The coreinsight is that minimum overlap is achieved by functions that balance theirautocorrelation structure while maintaining necessary flatness.\n\nKey improvements emerge from:\n- Moving beyond block-wise optimizations to consider continuous functions\n- Employing a multigrid strategy for simultaneous coarse-fine optimization\n- Incorporating adaptive barrier functions that penalize deviation from desiredoverlap patterns\n- Using mutual and self-interleave pairing to avoid discontinuous localmaxima\n\nThe method's advantage is its ability to escape shallow local minima common intemporal-harmonic strategies by considering the full correlation profile whilemaintaining integral constraints.\n\n2. Mathematical Specification\n\nVariables:\n- n (grid size): Hexagonal lattice pattern\n- h(x): Piecewise-defined approximating function\n- \u03b1 (multiplier): Balances constraint violation penalties\n- \u03b2 (weight): Controls correlation sensitivity\n\nObjective:\nMinimize max\u2096 \u222bh(x)(1-h(x+k))dx over all shifts k\n\nConstraints:\n- 0 \u2264 h(x) \u2264 1 \u2200x\n- \u222b\u2080\u00b2 h(x)dx = 1\n- Correlation penalties for undesirable overlap patterns\n\nOptimization:\nFormulate as:\n  minimize F(h) = max\u2096 [\u222bh(x)(1-h(x+k))dx] \nsubject to:\n  \u222bh(x)dx = 1\n  0 \u2264 h(x) \u2264 1\n\nwhere F(h) is approximated by:\n  F(h) \u2248 (2.0/n) * max\u2096 [\u27e8h, 1 - shift\u2096h\u27e9]\n\uff1a (1) with multigrid projection\n\n3. Implementation Procedure\n\nAlgorithm structure:\n\ndef run(seed,budget_s):\n    initialize lattice samples (n=310)\n    set temperature parameter = 0.7\n    initialize cooling schedule (factor=0.95, min_temp=0.1)\n    begin multigrid loop\n        coarsen grid (n_i = n * i^2 for i=0.1,0.3,0.5,0.8)\n        use projected gradient descent with barrier function\n        enforce repairment via energy minimization\n        temperature += cooling factor\n    end multigrid loop\n    return best solution found\n\nWith sample operations:\n\ndef evaluate_erdos(h):\n    n = len(h)\n    dx = 2.0/n\n    correlation = np.correlate(h, 1-h, mode=\"full\")\n    return np.max(correlation) * dx\n\ndef enforce_constraint(h, temperature):\n    # Compute violation energy:\n    sum_error = abs(np.sum(h*dx) - 1)\n    box_errors = np.sum(np.maximum(0, h-dt) + np.maximum(0, 1-h))\n    return temperature*(sum_error**2 + box_errors)\n\n4. Search Choices and Variations\n\nGrid sequence: \n  layers = [50, 100, 200, 310]   (fine to coarse)\nAlpha values: \n  [1.0, 3.0, 10.0, 30.0, 100.0] (growing barrier penalties)\n\nConstraints: \n  Primary integral: \u03a3 h_i * dx\u2081 = 0.5\n  Secondary distribution: quartiles must contain 5% tails\n\nCooling schedule: \n  Use simulated annealing (initial T=1.0) with exponential decay:\n      T_t = T\u2080 * 0.95^t_min\n  Continue until T_min or time exceeded (25% of budget)\n\n5. Compute Budget and Robustness\n\nResource allocation:\n  Coarsest grid (n=50): estimates 1 execution / day\n  Fullest grid (n=310): estimates 150,000 operations/second\n  Budget breakdown:\n      n=50: 500,000 operations\n      n=100: 2,000,000 operations\n      n=200: 5,000,000 operations\n      n=310: 15,000,000 operations\n\nTermination:\n  Systematically test with cooling factors [0.9, 0.95, 0.99] upon stall\n  Track best of last 50 evaluations \n  Return repair(h) at both T_minute and T_hour thresholds\n\n6. Validation and Return Contract\n\nFeasibility checks:\n  Validate: \u222bh(x)dx == 1 (with tolerance 1e-6)\n  Verify: 0 \u2264 h(x) \u2264 1 for all x \u2208 [0,2]\n  Check: correlation minima stabilize below 1e-4delta\n\nRepair function:\ndef repair(h, grid_size=0):\n    if grid_size>0: interpolate to grid\n    dx=2/grid_size\n    target = grid_size/2.0\n    total = np.sum(h) * dx\n    if abs(total - 0.5) > 1e-6:\n        h *= (0.5 - total) / (dx*(-target))   # adjust by scaling\n    return np.clip(h, 0.0, 1.0)\n\nObjective evaluation:\ndef compute_objective(h):\n    px = np.array([i*dx for i in range(len(h))])\n    py = np.array([1-h[i] for i in range(len(h))])\n    corr = np.correlate(h, py, mode='full')\n    # Evaluate maximum weighted lag\n    weights = [exp(-|k|/5) for k in range(len(corr))]\n    return max([c_i * w_i for c_i,w_i in zip(corr,weights)])",
